    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## Change: level rules \u2192 points system\n\nI replaced the direct level computation with a points system, exposing both `membershipPoints` and `membershipLevel`.\n\n**Points** (`MembershipLevels.pointsForOwner`): start at 0; `+2` email present, `+1` `namesakeCount == 0`, `+2` household of 3+ (`householdSize`), `+3` tenure over 365 days.\n\n**Level** (`MembershipLevels.forOwner`): mapped from points \u2014 `1` (0\u20131), `2` (2\u20133), `3` (4\u20135), `4` (6+).\n\nFiles touched:\n- `mapper/MembershipLevels.java` \u2014 new points method + points-derived level, replacing the old \"start at 1, cap at 3, +1 for tenure\" rule.\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 added the `membershipPoints` mapping alongside `membershipLevel`.\n- `resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added the `membershipPoints` property (drives the generated DTO field) and updated the `membershipLevel` description/range to `1\u20134`.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreReturnsPointsAndLevel`) \u2014 a fresh owner with an email, no namesake, single-member household, zero tenure \u2192 3 points, level 2 \u2014 passes, and `mvn test` reports **BUILD SUCCESS** (1 test class, 0 failures).",
