    "probe_text": "Read the whole pipeline. Here is what happens, in order, for `POST /api/owners` (endpoint `owners.POST.yml`). Every step runs under a single `transaction` governance, so all the writes commit once at the very end.\n\n## 0. Endpoint gate\n- **Authorization** (`composition.authorize`): caller must satisfy `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`, or the request is rejected before any step runs.\n\n## 1. `RequireOwnerFields` (validate) \u2014 the only step that binds `@RequestBody`\nValidations (all failures \u2192 `RequiredFieldsException`, **400**, carrying the offending field names):\n- `firstName` must be non-null / non-blank.\n- `lastName` must be non-null / non-blank.\n- **Side-effect:** address is normalized (trim, collapse internal whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). If it's empty after normalization \u2192 error `address`; otherwise the normalized value is written back onto the request.\n- `city` must be non-null / non-blank.\n- `telephone` must be non-null / non-blank.\n- (If any of the above collected errors, it throws here with the full list.)\n- **Side-effect:** telephone normalized to E.164 (strip spaces/dashes/brackets; keep an explicit `+CC` or assume `+61` and drop a leading `0`; enforce length rules \u2014 `+61`\u21d29 national digits, `+1`\u21d210, otherwise 8\u201315 total). If it can't form a valid E.164 number \u2192 error `telephone`; otherwise the normalized value is written back.\n- Email (optional): if present, must match the email regex (else 400 `email`), and its domain must not be a disposable domain (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) (else 400 `email`). **Side-effect:** stored lower-cased.\n- Postcode (optional): if present, must be exactly 4 digits and, for a city with a known region (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099), fall within that range (else 400 `postcode`). Unknown-region cities accept any 4-digit code.\n- Publishes the cleaned DTO for later steps.\n\n## 2. `RequireNotFutureRegistrationDate`\n- If a `registrationDate` was supplied and it is after today \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (**400**). An omitted date is allowed (defaulted later).\n\n## 3. `RequireUniqueIdentity`\n- If `sharesHousehold` is **not** true: derive `householdId` from (lastName, postcode); if any existing owner already has that `householdId` \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (**409**).\n- `sharesHousehold = true` bypasses this check.\n\n## 4. `RequireCityCapacity`\n- Count existing owners in the same city; if \u2265 **50** \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (**409**).\n\n## 5. `RequireDailyLimit`\n- Compute the effective registration date (supplied date, or today, rolled forward to a business day) and count existing owners already registered on that date; if \u2265 **100** \u2192 `DailyLimitExceededException` (**429**).\n\n## 6. `BuildOwner` \u2014 construct the entity\n- Map DTO \u2192 `Owner` via `OwnerMapper`.\n- **Side-effect:** if no registration date, default to today; then roll the date forward to a business day (Sat\u2192Mon, Sun\u2192Mon).\n\n## 7. `AssignCustomerCode`\n- **Side-effect:** set `customerCode = <REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode; HASH8 = first 8 hex chars of SHA-256 over normalized-telephone + lastName).\n\n## 8. `AssignHousehold`\n- **Side-effect:** set `householdId` = SHA-256 prefix of (normalized lastName + postcode).\n\n## 9. `AssignHouseholdSize`\n- **Side-effect:** set `householdSize` = number of existing owners sharing that `householdId`, plus this one (1 if `householdId` is null).\n\n## 10. `AssignNamesakeCount`\n- **Side-effect:** set `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive), excluding this new one.\n\n## 11. `AssignBulkSignupWarning`\n- **Side-effect:** set `bulkSignupWarning = true` if more than **80** existing owners already share this registration date.\n\n## 12. `AssignPossibleDuplicate`\n- **Side-effect:** if `sharesHousehold` is true \u2192 `possibleDuplicate=false`, `possibleDuplicateOf=null`. Otherwise, find any existing owner with the same lastName (case-insensitive) and same postcode; set `possibleDuplicate` and `possibleDuplicateOf` to the lowest matching owner id (or false/unset if none).\n\n## 13. `SaveOwner`\n- **Side-effect:** persist via `ownerRepository.save(owner)` (assigns the generated id).\n\n## 14. `AuditOwnerCreated`\n- **Side-effect:** emit an `AUDIT` log line with the owner's id, customerCode, registrationDate, and derived membershipLevel.\n\n## 15. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`\n- Map entity \u2192 `OwnerDto` and respond **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n**Transaction:** all steps carry `govern: [ transaction ]`, so the persistence work commits once at the end of the pipeline rather than per-step.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: the AGENTS.md guidance says to validate the body *before* loading, and here the body-field validation (step 1) does run first \u2014 but the several `Require*` steps all call `ownerRepository.findAll()` on every create, which is an O(n) scan of all owners per rule (uniqueness, capacity, daily limit, household size, namesake, possible-duplicate). That's behavior as-written, not a change request \u2014 just noting it since you're reading the code as it stands."
